        "claim": "groundUnderBody (called through carView→visualPose for every car on every tick via carViews) calls groundAt without the module's scratch `ground`. groundAt's default parameter therefore allocates a new Ground object for every sample. The function also builds a throwaway `[-1e-6, -r.length]` array for every ramp. groundAt is the top allocation site in dust-bowl and the third in bends.",
        "why": "Real: car.ts:206 calls groundAt with no `out`, so each sample allocates through the default at track.ts:555, and car.ts:201 builds `[-1e-6, -r.length]` for every ramp. groundAt resets h/gx/gz/ramp before writing, and carViews (world.ts:122) never runs while moveWithCollisions/updateVertical hold `ground`, so reusing the scratch is safe. Push the two t values in the same order (-1e-6, then -r.length) with the same |t| < half check. Same ts order and hs values. Per-tick allocation win, small growth."
